WEBVTT

02:17.400 --> 02:19.770
That sounded pretty rad.

02:19.800 --> 02:21.500
As expected of you, Riki.

02:22.270 --> 02:23.610
I still have a long way to go.

02:23.640 --> 02:25.540
My cornerings were unstable.

02:25.980 --> 02:27.580
I'll go for another lap.

02:30.350 --> 02:32.220
Don't get too carried away!

02:32.250 --> 02:32.950
Hey!

02:32.980 --> 02:34.320
Go for it!

02:34.980 --> 02:39.360
Sheesh. You're not a speeder.

02:39.560 --> 02:42.860
Oh well, it's good he's such a perfectionist.

02:42.890 --> 02:44.930
People are looking up to him.

02:52.100 --> 02:56.670
Is that the only reason he's trying so hard?

03:03.780 --> 03:07.080
Hey, the airbike race is nice and all,

03:07.120 --> 03:10.690
but let's go see the pet auction held at Mistral Park.

03:11.420 --> 03:13.090
Auction, huh?

03:13.120 --> 03:14.920
We're just going to watch.

03:14.960 --> 03:16.690
It's good to get down...

03:16.690 --> 03:19.630
...and cheer your head off with the crowd once in a while.

03:22.130 --> 03:25.500
There'll be swarms of country people there too.

03:25.540 --> 03:29.440
If we're lucky, we might even be able to get some drinking money.

03:32.140 --> 03:36.080
Riki, Kirie says he wants to go watch the pet auction.

03:36.110 --> 03:38.950
You guys can go if you want. I'll pass.

03:38.980 --> 03:41.180
What's wrong? You suck.

03:41.220 --> 03:43.950
It's not like you have anything better to do.

03:45.350 --> 03:49.830
Or... is there a particular reason why you don't want to go?

03:49.860 --> 03:51.730
I'm just not interested.

03:51.760 --> 03:52.900
Is that all?

03:52.930 --> 03:53.700
What?

03:54.960 --> 03:58.840
Is there someone you'd rather not meet there?

03:58.900 --> 04:00.440
Not really.

04:01.140 --> 04:02.640
Well, we're decided then.

04:02.670 --> 04:05.410
Let's go for a group outing!

04:05.440 --> 04:08.850
Nothing interesting's gonna happen if we stay here anyway.

04:10.210 --> 04:12.680
Let's start something new!

04:12.720 --> 04:14.380
Something new!

05:15.040 --> 05:19.320
I processed 584 cases in 9 minutes.

05:22.050 --> 05:26.990
As data analysis speed, that's not bad.

05:28.120 --> 05:34.560
If I'm not in a hurry, this is less of a burden on my body

05:34.560 --> 05:38.870
than using the brain gear.

06:05.600 --> 06:07.830
When did you get back from Kiira?

06:08.300 --> 06:09.530
Yesterday.

06:10.770 --> 06:13.370
You're busy as always.

06:14.100 --> 06:15.870
Not as busy as you.

06:17.440 --> 06:26.120
Speaking of which, I heard that your prototype is going to be at the pet auction this time.

06:26.150 --> 06:29.590
That's right. Two Seraphim models.

06:29.650 --> 06:30.950
Male and female pair?

06:30.990 --> 06:35.830
No, but breeding is still possible.

06:36.330 --> 06:40.260
I expect the opening price would also be of a different league to the others.

06:40.300 --> 06:43.930
Why don't you get one, male or female, whichever you prefer.

06:44.700 --> 06:47.670
Isn't it time for you to buy a new pet?

06:55.680 --> 06:57.980
It's already been half a year since then.

06:58.010 --> 07:01.580
No, has it only been half a year?

07:02.990 --> 07:06.820
As the Elites, it's our duty to buy pets.

07:06.860 --> 07:11.060
The serving Furniture will die of boredom.

07:11.630 --> 07:19.000
You're right. Perhaps it would be good to have a look at the prototype which you are so proud of.

07:20.340 --> 07:22.740
But it will depend on my schedule.

07:47.130 --> 07:48.100
Norris!

07:48.160 --> 07:49.300
Here, here!

07:54.800 --> 07:58.470
When it comes to bike parts, Max's your man.

07:58.510 --> 08:02.810
They're made well, but there's still a limit to these parts.

08:04.180 --> 08:07.120
I'll sell custom parts for around 1,200.

08:07.150 --> 08:08.380
That's too much.

08:08.420 --> 08:11.120
They're just parts you'd throw away if you can't sell!

08:11.150 --> 08:12.990
If you don't like it, then you can trade other parts.

08:13.020 --> 08:15.320
I have loads of other spares.

08:15.320 --> 08:18.390
That's low! You're always like this!

08:18.390 --> 08:23.570
Didn't imagine that Norris' true love was such a rough old man.

08:32.170 --> 08:33.280
This is...

08:34.940 --> 08:38.250
An Eos security guard robot...

08:38.280 --> 08:39.620
I can't believe it.

08:43.150 --> 08:46.420
No... this is just junk.

08:46.460 --> 08:48.290
There's something wrong with me.

08:48.320 --> 08:53.600
There's no way an android used by Tanagyra would end up here.

08:54.700 --> 09:00.640
Damn... it's all because Kirie started talking about going to the pet auction.

09:01.400 --> 09:05.540
I get it, it's okay. Please, I'm counting on you.

09:05.570 --> 09:07.280
Deal?

09:07.880 --> 09:09.010
Yeah.

09:09.050 --> 09:12.250
Hey Riki, is there anything else you want?

09:12.520 --> 09:13.550
Nah.

09:18.150 --> 09:20.060
Riki, wait up.

09:22.120 --> 09:23.490
What?

09:23.530 --> 09:25.160
You and Guy...

09:26.030 --> 09:27.900
What's up between you two?

09:27.960 --> 09:30.270
Nah, I'm fine...

09:30.300 --> 09:33.240
You haven't broken the pairing, have you?

09:33.270 --> 09:37.040
I know this isn't my business,

09:37.040 --> 09:40.410
but it's better to end things properly.

09:42.650 --> 09:44.150
You're right.

09:44.210 --> 09:48.380
Well, Max's gonna get jealous if we talk too long.

09:49.050 --> 09:50.150
See ya round!

10:03.500 --> 10:06.540
I can't go on like this...

11:25.950 --> 11:29.750
Yay! The day has come!

11:29.790 --> 11:32.090
Shut the hell up and ride!

11:32.120 --> 11:35.490
Woohoo! Yahoo!

11:36.460 --> 11:38.460
Let's fly, let's fly!

11:38.460 --> 11:40.560
Let's go!!

12:01.680 --> 12:04.250
All right, let's go.

12:21.970 --> 12:24.670
Yeah! Midas is a great place!

12:24.670 --> 12:26.040
So full of life!

12:26.080 --> 12:29.550
Come on guys, get into it!

12:29.580 --> 12:30.750
Let's go!

12:34.750 --> 12:37.820
That kid Kirie's really excited right now.

12:37.890 --> 12:42.660
He's so enthusiastic, taking us all to a pet auction.

12:43.290 --> 12:44.790
Because he's a kid.

12:45.390 --> 12:48.130
Come on, hurry up!

12:48.900 --> 12:50.930
We'll leave without you!

12:50.930 --> 12:52.570
A kid, huh?

12:52.600 --> 12:53.670
What?

12:53.700 --> 12:56.710
Nothing, just thought of the past.

12:56.710 --> 12:57.840
Of what?

12:58.640 --> 13:06.350
When we were still in the Colony and heard that the Academy were releasing pets, we got super excited too.

13:06.850 --> 13:12.190
I think you were the most excited out of us all.

13:12.250 --> 13:14.590
I forgot about that.

13:14.620 --> 13:18.260
You were a lot like how Kirie is now.

13:18.290 --> 13:21.030
Don't compare me to that brat.

13:21.100 --> 13:25.730
Ah. Well you were a bit more mature.

13:25.770 --> 13:31.540
You were afraid I'd get lost, so you kept holding onto my han-

13:34.080 --> 13:36.010
Ouch! What was that for?

13:36.050 --> 13:38.710
Just when all these great memories were coming back to me.

13:39.580 --> 13:41.350
Hey, wait!

13:52.930 --> 13:56.700
This is what an auction's like... full of hot energy.

13:57.470 --> 14:04.840
Heh, auctions... it's just a gathering of uncultured perverts.

14:04.870 --> 14:09.210
But they're potentially good clients for us.

14:11.750 --> 14:14.050
It's pretty lively here.

14:14.080 --> 14:15.680
Of course.

14:15.680 --> 14:20.090
There are a lot of new lines this time from crossbreeding.

14:20.490 --> 14:26.230
I wonder what they're thinking when they charge so much for these ugly monsters.

14:26.260 --> 14:29.160
Hey Riki, what do you think?

14:32.000 --> 14:34.340
Everyone thinks that at first.

14:34.370 --> 14:36.970
"Would I tap that?"

14:37.310 --> 14:41.410
And then, when you hear the lowest offer price for the pet,

14:41.440 --> 14:43.580
you'll suddenly come to your senses.

14:43.610 --> 14:50.250
In the end, you'll be weary of the divide between yourself and the rich.

14:59.260 --> 15:03.170
Heh, just because you're a bit older, you already think like an old man?

15:03.200 --> 15:04.930
Not again...

15:04.970 --> 15:07.900
Why don't they ever get along?

15:07.940 --> 15:10.310
Kirie never learns his lesson.

15:10.340 --> 15:13.410
He can't act like such a kid forever.

15:13.440 --> 15:17.450
In other words, even with the charisma of being the top dog of the Slum,

15:17.480 --> 15:21.520
you become extremely mediocre after three years.

15:21.550 --> 15:23.590
I'm disappointed.

15:23.620 --> 15:24.320
You!

15:25.450 --> 15:27.290
That hurt.

15:27.320 --> 15:29.260
What was that?

15:29.690 --> 15:32.190
That's enough, you moron!

15:32.230 --> 15:34.760
What's wrong with telling the truth?

15:35.500 --> 15:36.630
This is Midas.

15:36.630 --> 15:38.370
It's not our territory.

15:38.400 --> 15:42.770
Don't speak of the Slum so loudly, retard!

15:42.810 --> 15:44.270
You wanna get caught by the police?

15:44.940 --> 15:49.040
How would they know what we're talking about

15:49.080 --> 15:51.910
when there's all sorts of foreigners gathered here?

15:51.950 --> 15:55.550
Look! Nobody's taking any notice of us!

15:55.580 --> 15:57.120
Don't be so scared!

15:58.020 --> 16:02.560
You have no right to speak in a loud voice; you're only scavenging Bison's leftovers.

16:02.620 --> 16:06.400
Wait till you become a real man before you say those words.

16:06.960 --> 16:09.730
I just don't want to play myself cheap!

16:09.770 --> 16:13.340
Then shut your dirty mouth.

16:13.840 --> 16:15.240
It's obnoxious.

16:15.300 --> 16:17.310
Let's leave it here.

16:17.340 --> 16:18.840
Come on, let's go.

16:20.140 --> 16:22.540
That's enough from you, kid.

16:25.080 --> 16:29.650
Seriously, pick a fight with Riki? In another hundred years.

16:30.050 --> 16:33.320
Lucky enough that he didn't piss his pants.

16:33.360 --> 16:36.760
Oh well, he should be grateful we stopped him.

16:38.890 --> 16:41.830
Why do I have to put up with this?!

16:41.860 --> 16:43.830
It's because that you don't even understand this,

16:43.870 --> 16:46.130
that's why you're a brat.

16:46.200 --> 16:47.370
Stop calling me a brat or a kid!

16:47.400 --> 16:51.770
You guys couldn't even bring back Bison!

16:51.840 --> 16:54.480
You're just old men throwing your lives away!

16:54.510 --> 16:55.480
Shit!

16:55.510 --> 16:58.280
You're just a bunch of sore losers.

17:25.210 --> 17:28.840
What, is that an elitist party?

17:29.580 --> 17:32.350
No, it looks like a pet auction.

17:34.550 --> 17:37.650
That's why I said you're old men with no balls.

17:38.050 --> 17:39.120
Wow.

17:39.150 --> 17:42.120
The rich are on a totally a different league.

17:42.190 --> 17:44.190
It's like a different dimension.

17:44.530 --> 17:48.930
Oh well, can't do nothing but laugh at the gap now.

17:51.630 --> 17:53.940
We're mongrels of the Slum.

17:53.970 --> 17:56.070
We've got nothing to lose.

17:56.870 --> 17:59.540
If I had just one chance...

18:00.280 --> 18:04.010
I might be able to grab the scrapped ends of an opportunity.

18:04.780 --> 18:07.880
The chance of climbing up isn't zero.

18:16.530 --> 18:20.800
Even though there are losers who would waste three whole years...

18:23.070 --> 18:26.840
Well, we've seen the other dimension of those of a different rank.

18:27.000 --> 18:28.400
It's about time to go back.

18:28.440 --> 18:31.040
Yeah, I'm hungry.

18:33.440 --> 18:36.410
Hey! Why don't we go cruising?

18:36.410 --> 18:38.380
It's safer not to try.

18:38.410 --> 18:39.480
You scared?

18:39.510 --> 18:43.290
Idiot, the number of police around these days is no joke!

18:43.320 --> 18:44.620
It's dangerous.

18:44.650 --> 18:47.190
But we can't go back empty-handed!

18:47.220 --> 18:49.190
I won't stop you if you want to do it.

18:49.220 --> 18:53.360
We're not the ones suffering when you get caught.

18:54.400 --> 18:57.930
You don't even have the pride to do something bold?

19:29.200 --> 19:32.170
Wow, royal class.

19:35.600 --> 19:38.510
No way... isn't that... Tanagura's...

19:38.610 --> 19:39.610
Blondie...?

19:40.140 --> 19:41.180
Riki...

19:41.580 --> 19:42.440
For real?

19:42.480 --> 19:44.510
Really? It's him in person?

20:00.100 --> 20:03.870
Hey! Moron, why are you hiding?

20:03.930 --> 20:05.900
It's just so sudden...

20:07.200 --> 20:08.100
Hey...

20:18.150 --> 20:20.520
This has gotta be a joke...

20:25.990 --> 20:27.060
Riki...

20:28.490 --> 20:29.690
You okay?

20:30.560 --> 20:31.960
Why...

20:36.970 --> 20:37.930
Not yet.

20:39.770 --> 20:42.140
Don't make me say the same thing twice.

20:49.240 --> 20:53.080
You are my pet.

20:55.520 --> 20:56.920
I can't...

20:57.490 --> 20:58.620
No...

21:00.990 --> 21:03.990
Wow! Amazing!

21:03.990 --> 21:06.230
It's an Elite from Tanagura!

21:06.260 --> 21:07.630
And it's a Blondie!

21:07.660 --> 21:10.700
You hardly see one in real life!

21:11.430 --> 21:13.340
This might be my chance...

21:13.800 --> 21:16.910
Hey, it's really time to go home.

21:16.940 --> 21:19.670
It's gotten kind of rowdy.

21:21.710 --> 21:22.510
Hey.

21:22.540 --> 21:23.350
Oh!

21:27.950 --> 21:30.820
If only I had a chance, I'd...

21:35.360 --> 21:37.960
But how...

21:38.360 --> 21:41.300
Come on, Kirie! We're going without you!

22:07.290 --> 22:08.790
Did you call for me?

22:12.190 --> 22:13.400
This is...?

22:20.940 --> 22:23.570
Do you know who that is?

22:23.610 --> 22:24.810
No.

22:24.840 --> 22:26.440
I see.

22:26.470 --> 22:28.640
Is he a mongrel of the Slum?

22:29.010 --> 22:30.580
Try him.

22:30.610 --> 22:31.750
Huh?

22:33.650 --> 22:38.390
You mean, let him be an errand boy at the market?

22:38.420 --> 22:42.360
No, I meant to make him your underling.

22:42.890 --> 22:44.990
Mine...?

22:45.030 --> 22:46.430
That's right.

22:46.460 --> 22:50.400
Educate him well.

22:50.430 --> 22:53.240
What work should I give him?

22:53.270 --> 22:55.670
And how should we change the way we interact with him.

22:55.700 --> 22:59.240
So that it's possible to cut ties with him at any time.

23:00.810 --> 23:02.480
Understood.

23:04.950 --> 23:08.880
Should I start now?

23:09.050 --> 23:10.190
That's fine.

23:10.220 --> 23:14.990
Contact Pen 7 of the auction house.

23:15.060 --> 23:17.730
Thank you very much.

23:29.040 --> 23:32.340
He doesn't question more than he needs to.

23:32.370 --> 23:34.940
He's just as professional as always.

23:34.980 --> 23:37.380
What should I do now?

23:40.920 --> 23:43.950
This was an unimaginable encounter.

23:43.990 --> 23:48.890
Well, it was going to happen sooner or later.
